241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 82 0 R
/T (For a phased-in pre-existing condition sharing need, the sharing amounts are cumulative. For example, if a member receives $5,000 in sharing for a pre-existing condition during Year 1, they would have up to $25,000 of additional sharing available for that same pre-existing condition in Year 2. If they use the $25k in Year 2, then in Year 3, they have $45k toward the same pre-existing need. In Year 4, for the same pre-existing need, they will be eligible for $75K in sharing \(150-75\). The maximum sharing for a repeat need in years 1-4 is $75k.)
/E (For a phased-in pre-existing condition sharing need, the sharing amounts are cumulative. For example, if a member receives $5,000 in sharing for a pre-existing condition during Year 1, they would have up to $25,000 of additional sharing available for that same pre-existing condition in Year 2. If they use the $25k in Year 2, then in Year 3, they have $45k toward the same pre-existing need. In Year 4, for the same pre-existing need, they will be eligible for $75K in sharing \(150-75\). The maximum sharing for a repeat need in years 1-4 is $75k.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [16]
>>
